From 2749eaae98157a2ec1fb670fded8bc69d21f37df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias <ruck.tobias@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 May 2021 06:27:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 098/196] Implement Malfix (#171)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Builds on the separation of txid and txhash (thanks Amaury!):
- txhash retains its old behavior
- txid is H(version || MerkleRoot(∀: input.prevout || input.sequence) || height(inputs merkle tree) || MerkleRoot(outputs) || height(outputs merkle tree) || locktime)
- txid is what transactions commit to in prevouts
- Blocks commit to H(txhash || txid) in the leaves of the merkle root
- Fix CVE-2012-2459 by using 0x0000...000000 instead of repeating the hash for layers with an odd number of hashes
- Coinbase txid is now made unique through an OP_RETURN output at vout=1 instead of in the scriptSig, as scriptSigs are no longer covered in txid.

This change allows two new things:
- Malleability fix; allows commitments to chains of txs without any party being able to unilaterally break the validity of the chain by altering txids
- Introspection of input txs, allowing inductive proofs, which e.g. can be used to construct miner-enforced tokens
